librtlsdr: add rtlsdr_open_fd() for Android USB-OTG

Android applications cannot open /dev/bus/usb nodes, so the device file
descriptor is obtained in Java (UsbDeviceConnection.getFileDescriptor()) and
handed to native code. Disable libusb device discovery, wrap the descriptor
with libusb_wrap_sys_device(), and run the normal claim/probe sequence.

The claim/probe tail of rtlsdr_open() is split into rtlsdr_init_opened_device()
so both open paths share it verbatim.

Generated against rtl-sdr v2.0.3 (797f8143266d983c56d8f35d2d442527529dd8a5).

